title: vCenter rsyslog Path Traversal to Cron Drop (CVE-2026-59310)
id: 8f2c1a90-3b7d-4e2a-9c4f-1d6b5e0a7c31
status: experimental
description: >
  Detects exploitation of the rsyslog path-traversal-to-RCE issue in vCenter
  (lab scenario CVE-2026-59310). Covers both the crafted-hostname traversal
  indicator and the resulting cron-file write / rsyslog-spawned shell.
references:
  - GraySentinel DSOU Day 1 lab scenario (CVE number is lab scaffolding; verify against vendor advisory before production use)
author: Eswar Mahalingam
date: 2026/09/09
logsource:
  product: linux
detection:
  traversal_indicator:
    service: syslog
    message|contains:
      - '../'
      - '..%2f'
  cron_write:
    service: auditd
    syscall: 257            # openat
    path|startswith: '/etc/cron.d/'
  rsyslog_child_shell:
    service: auditd
    ParentProcessName|endswith: 'rsyslogd'
    ProcessName|endswith:
      - '/sh'
      - '/bash'
  condition: traversal_indicator or cron_write or rsyslog_child_shell
level: critical
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate configuration management writing to /etc/cron.d/
  - Rsyslog templates that legitimately contain '../' in message bodies
tags:
  - attack.initial_access
  - attack.persistence
  - attack.t1053.003
